MediaTek MT6639 (MT7927) LE Audio: pick the ISO interface alt setting
that actually exists.

MTK_ISO_IFNUM (interface 2) exposes a single alt setting (0) on 13d3:3588,
but __set_mtk_intr_interface() hardcoded alt setting 1, so USB rejected it
with EINVAL and the ISO data path never came up:

    Bluetooth: hci0: setting interface failed (22)
    Bluetooth: hci0: ISO intf not support (-19)
    Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x2062 failed: -110   (LE Set CIG Parameters)

Without ISO there is no LE Audio: BlueZ's BAP transport acquisition fails
(org.bluez.Error.Failed) and LC3 can never be negotiated.

Taken from upstream ("Bluetooth: btmtk: ..." in v7.2, which additionally
uses usb_find_common_endpoints(); that refactor is equivalent to the open-
coded endpoint loop here, so only the alt-setting choice is backported).

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c
@@ -1023,7 +1023,8 @@
 	if (!btmtk_data->isopkt_intf)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	err = usb_set_interface(btmtk_data->udev, MTK_ISO_IFNUM, 1);
+	err = usb_set_interface(btmtk_data->udev, MTK_ISO_IFNUM,
+			       (intf->num_altsetting > 1) ? 1 : 0);
 	if (err < 0) {
 		bt_dev_err(hdev, "setting interface failed (%d)", -err);
 		return err;
